
>> servings: 2

Make @jasmine rice{1%cup}.

In a bowl, mix @soya sauce{3%tbsp} and @sesame seed oil{1%tsp}.

Cut @chicken strips{500%g} into cubes, and mix with @baking soda{3/4%tsp} in a container. Seal container and leave in fridge for ~{20%minutes}.

Chop @onion{1}, @carrots{3}, @baby cabbage{1}, @brocollini{200%g}, and @spring onions{2}.

Remove chicken from fridge, rinse thoroughly and strain.

Head up @olive oil{1%tbsp} and @sesame seed oil{1%tsp} in a #pan{}. Add the chicken and cook until cook through. It does not have to be crispy. Remove and put aside.

In same pan, add @olive oil{1%tbsp} and @sesame seed oil{1%tsp}.

Add onions and cook until soft.

Add @garlic{3%clove} and grated @ginger{1%nub} and finely chopped @chilli{1}. Cook until fragrant.

Add carrots, baby cabbage, brocollini and white parts of spring onion. Cook until soft.

In a separate pan, scramble @eggs{3}.

Add eggs to main pan.

Add rice and stir.

Add chicken and stir.

Add soya sauce mixture and stir.
